From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a webview's new window keeps the size its page
 asked for

`window.open(url, name, "width=640,height=420")` in a browser window
reached WebViewGuest::AddNewContents at 1x1 on a headless engine:
ShowCreatedWindow fits the requested bounds to the screen nearest the
opener, and a guest's screen there is 1x1. The shell sizes and places
browser windows itself, so it needs the size the page asked for.

- ShowCreatedWindow keeps the requested size for a guest's new window.
  The display it picks, and the fullscreen drop on it, are unchanged.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
index 8b353ce..cd7b9ec 100644
--- a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
@@ -6174,6 +6174,12 @@ WebContents* WebContentsImpl::ShowCreatedWindow(
   // TODO(crbug.com/40092782): Utilize window_features.has_x and others.
   blink::mojom::WindowFeatures adjusted_features = window_features;
   int64_t display_id = AdjustWindowRect(&adjusted_features.bounds, opener);
+  // DOMICILE: a guest's new window keeps the size its page asked for. The
+  // shell sizes and places browser windows, and fitting the size to the
+  // guest's screen can shrink it (to 1x1 on a headless engine).
+  if (GetBrowserPluginGuest()) {
+    adjusted_features.bounds.set_size(window_features.bounds.size());
+  }
 
   // Drop fullscreen when opening a WebContents to prohibit deceptive behavior.
   // Only drop fullscreen on the specific destination display, if it is known.
